From: lzx <lzx@local>
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] mm: guide effective-tier protection with myfs app priors

Use the atomic application prediction state delivered through /dev/myfs to
add a bounded, positive-only bias to effective-tier scoring. Keep the native
pressure gates and page budgets, expose action counters and trace provenance,
and add a dedicated compile-time ablation switch.

Signed-off-by: lzx <lzx@local>
---
--- a/mm/parp/Kconfig
+++ b/mm/parp/Kconfig
@@ -98,4 +98,15 @@
 	  KUnit runtime and reclaim-lock latency gates have passed. When disabled,
 	  every APPLY mode setter returns -EOPNOTSUPP.
 
+config PARP_APP_PRIOR_TIER_PROTECT # lzx-note
+	bool "Guide effective-tier protection with /dev/myfs app priors"
+	depends on PARP_EFFECTIVE_TIER && PARP_MYFS
+	default n
+	help
+	  Add a bounded, positive-only bias from the atomic /dev/myfs application
+	  prediction state to the per-page reuse score. The foreground application
+	  and LSTM Top-3 candidates receive rank-calibrated protection, while the
+	  existing effective-tier pressure gates and page budgets remain mandatory.
+	  Disable this option for a compile-time application-prior ablation.
+
 endmenu # lzx-note
